WEBVTT

00:10.490 --> 00:13.930
No!

00:20.720 --> 00:23.150
Oh, there you are!

00:25.690 --> 00:28.380
Jougo!

00:33.590 --> 00:36.040
Looks like most of your body's back.

00:36.660 --> 00:39.610
Yeah, this place is relaxing.

00:39.610 --> 00:41.880
Humans don't come anywhere near it.

00:41.880 --> 00:44.930
Lacking a body really is a problem.

00:44.930 --> 00:47.790
It makes self-preservation so inefficient.

00:47.790 --> 00:52.330
Mahito, you're awfully worn down yourself.

00:52.330 --> 00:54.150
Oh, you could tell?

00:54.150 --> 00:57.960
Sukuna and his vessel 
are my natural enemies.

00:58.760 --> 01:02.970
I started this game because 
I happened to acquire a new toy,

01:03.690 --> 01:05.890
but it just didn't go so well.

01:05.890 --> 01:07.460
It was great at first, though.

01:07.750 --> 01:12.470
Are you sure I shouldn't have just 
used a hostage to force him into a pact?

01:12.470 --> 01:17.100
Like, "Hand your body over to Sukuna 
if you don't want to see him killed."

01:18.720 --> 01:23.280
No, pacts are only placed 
by oneself on oneself.

01:23.280 --> 01:27.500
It's not easy to forge pacts with others, 
or due to intervention from others.

01:29.780 --> 01:34.770
Maybe I should have just given that thing 
a lethal wound instead of transfiguring it.

01:35.030 --> 01:38.650
Then Sukuna might have been able to heal 
it with his reverse cursed technique.

01:40.130 --> 01:44.000
Know your place, fool.

01:44.790 --> 01:47.540
No, not with that personality.

01:47.540 --> 01:49.810
I think he would have refused either way.

01:51.210 --> 01:52.380
Jougo...

01:52.940 --> 01:55.200
Touching Sukuna made me realize that

01:55.200 --> 01:58.380
we should probably proceed 
with Getou's plan for now.

01:58.830 --> 02:01.460
Sukuna is that valuable.

02:03.890 --> 02:08.820
Gather all the fingers and 
offer them to Sukuna, huh?

02:09.990 --> 02:15.980
Even if we're all wiped out in the process, eh?

02:16.940 --> 02:18.480
Very well.

02:18.480 --> 02:22.660
I don't need to be the one laughing 
in the wasteland a century from now.

02:22.660 --> 02:25.960
As long as curses stand there as 
people, that's all that matters.

02:26.190 --> 02:28.460
Oh, you get it!

02:28.700 --> 02:33.000
Then first, let's go retrieve the 
six fingers Jujutsu Tech has.

02:33.000 --> 02:34.420
Is that necessary?

02:34.820 --> 02:37.640
The sorcerers are only 
keeping Itadori Yuuji around

02:37.640 --> 02:40.590
so he can take in Sukuna's fingers, right?

02:40.590 --> 02:42.720
He'll still eat them, even if we leave them be.

02:43.040 --> 02:44.610
The higher-ups at Jujutsu Tech

02:44.610 --> 02:48.300
are struggling to measure 
Itadori Yuuji's strength as a vessel,

02:48.760 --> 02:51.710
to see how many he can take 
before he goes berserk.

02:51.890 --> 02:55.480
They won't let him take them in 
until they've gathered all the fingers...

02:56.460 --> 02:58.500
With just one exception.

02:57.230 --> 03:01.740
Exception

02:59.030 --> 03:01.740
I want to feed them to him right away!

03:01.740 --> 03:03.960
And we can't wait that long, right?

03:03.960 --> 03:08.390
Worst case, there's also a chance 
they'll eliminate Itadori Yuuji.

03:08.810 --> 03:11.500
Into the tiger's den, huh?

03:11.960 --> 03:14.180
Well, what should we do, then?

03:14.450 --> 03:16.000
I've already taken steps.

03:16.280 --> 03:20.890
That's why I allowed Jujutsu Tech 
to retrieve the fingers we had.

04:44.050 --> 04:47.800
JUJUTSU KAISEN

04:55.440 --> 05:02.440
Episode 14: Kyoto Sister School Exchange Event - Group Battle 0 -

04:55.440 --> 05:02.440
Episode 14: Kyoto Sister School Exchange Event - Group Battle 0 -

04:59.040 --> 05:04.400
Nanami, talk about something interesting.

05:06.240 --> 05:07.880
Okay, I've got it!

05:07.890 --> 05:11.380
Let's play catch with discarded rice balls

05:11.380 --> 05:13.760
while discussing the separation of church and state!

05:13.760 --> 05:16.010
Let's post a video of it and troll people.

05:17.870 --> 05:20.030
Enjoy that on your own.

05:20.030 --> 05:21.890
What kind of idea is that?

05:23.450 --> 05:27.840
Drinking game time! Name things 
you love about Gojou Satoru!

05:28.630 --> 05:29.840
Everything!

05:31.020 --> 05:33.310
Please keep that attitude going.

05:33.850 --> 05:37.960
Itadori-kun needs that
kind of idiocy right now.

05:39.730 --> 05:42.650
You'll take on and complete 
several harder missions.

05:43.780 --> 05:47.900
That wasn't what I meant by "harder," though.

05:48.360 --> 05:52.210
Nanami, does Yuuji know about 
that finger in Yoshino's—

05:52.210 --> 05:53.380
I haven't told him.

05:53.890 --> 05:57.220
Knowing him, he'd just feel 
unnecessarily responsible.

05:57.820 --> 05:59.920
I'm glad I left you in charge.

06:00.140 --> 06:01.540
And the finger?

06:02.890 --> 06:05.450
I submitted it to the higher-ups, of course.

06:05.450 --> 06:08.990
If I gave it to you, you'd just 
feed it to Itadori-kun, right?

06:08.990 --> 06:09.750
Tsk.

06:09.750 --> 06:13.530
But is it really okay to bring him back?

06:14.030 --> 06:16.930
If the fact that he's alive becomes 
known at the exchange event,

06:16.930 --> 06:19.440
won't the higher-ups just target him again?

06:19.440 --> 06:22.300
Even if they do, Yuuji will be just fine now.

06:22.300 --> 06:24.950
You know that better than anyone, don't you?

06:27.560 --> 06:29.000
Sensei!

06:30.920 --> 06:32.660
Oh, Nanamin's here, too.

06:32.660 --> 06:33.540
Well, c'mon!

06:33.760 --> 06:36.040
Let's hurry up and go see everyone!

06:36.200 --> 06:37.210
So excited!

06:36.290 --> 06:41.630
"I thought you were dead..."
Touching Reunion
With Friends

06:37.720 --> 06:38.720
So excited!

06:37.750 --> 06:41.630
"Nice to meet you!!"
Deciding Factor of His First Impression,
First Meeting With the Second Years

06:38.720 --> 06:40.060
So excited!

06:39.210 --> 06:41.630
Kyoto Students Appear!!
Exchange Event Begins!
"Beginner's Guide to
the Exchange Event"

06:40.320 --> 06:41.340
So excited!

06:41.340 --> 06:46.660
Yuuji, are you planning to just show up 
like normal after dragging it out this long?

06:46.660 --> 06:48.180
Huh? I can't?!

06:48.960 --> 06:51.290
Even among sorcerers,

06:51.290 --> 06:55.370
you rarely see someone say they've actually 
been alive two whole months after they died.

06:55.370 --> 06:57.050
We have to make it a surprise!

06:57.980 --> 06:59.670
A surprise?

06:59.670 --> 07:01.890
Just leave it to me.

07:05.640 --> 07:09.110
The first-years will be laughing 
and crying from happiness and shock.

07:07.980 --> 07:08.880
I'm so glad!

07:08.880 --> 07:09.550
You're alive!

07:09.110 --> 07:11.280
The second-years and Kyoto 
students will cry with them.

07:09.550 --> 07:12.710
Thank goodness! Thank goodness!

07:11.280 --> 07:14.100
And someone among them 
will choke up and vomit,

07:12.710 --> 07:16.200
Blegh!

07:15.200 --> 07:18.590
and in the end, it'll even solve global warming!

07:18.590 --> 07:20.510
Cool!

07:21.560 --> 07:23.010
Sweet!

07:23.170 --> 07:24.340
What do I do?!

07:24.340 --> 07:26.520
Sensei, what should I do?!

07:26.520 --> 07:28.190
You don't have to do anything!

07:28.190 --> 07:31.520
Just do exactly as I say, 
and go with the flow!

07:31.520 --> 07:33.620
So what should I do?!

07:33.620 --> 07:36.480
Just go with the flow!

07:33.630 --> 07:36.480
It'll be enough of a surprise 
just to see he's alive.

07:36.760 --> 07:37.970
Kyoto
Come have fun in Kyoto
The Complete Guide

07:37.200 --> 07:37.970
What?!

07:38.390 --> 07:40.980
Why are you all empty-handed?!

07:42.170 --> 07:44.500
What are you doing with all that luggage?

07:44.500 --> 07:47.690
What do you mean? 
We're going to Kyoto, right?

07:47.270 --> 07:48.820
Fortunes

07:47.690 --> 07:51.010
For the exchange event 
with our sister school in Kyoto?

07:51.010 --> 07:54.430
It's an exchange event with 
our sister school in Kyoto.

07:54.430 --> 07:55.730
Held in Tokyo.

07:54.990 --> 07:56.490
Ueno Specialty

07:54.990 --> 07:56.490
Panda

07:56.750 --> 07:58.950
No way!

07:59.190 --> 08:02.220
What did I make all those 
preparations for, then?!

07:59.190 --> 08:02.220
No wonder our conversations 
have been a bit off lately.

08:02.220 --> 08:03.020
Yeah.

08:02.220 --> 08:04.940
I was totally ready to go sightseeing!

08:03.020 --> 08:04.010
Salmon.

08:04.010 --> 08:06.780
It's held at the school that 
won in the previous year.

08:04.940 --> 08:06.950
This sucks! What a scam!

08:06.950 --> 08:08.970
Then don't go winning, you idiots!

08:08.970 --> 08:11.320
We weren't in it last year!

08:11.320 --> 08:14.440
Only Yuuta participated to 
make the numbers match up!

08:14.440 --> 08:16.480
That was prior to freeing Rika.

08:16.770 --> 08:18.650
Apparently, it was an overwhelming win.

08:18.650 --> 08:20.760
I didn't see it, though,
since it was held in Kyoto.

08:21.470 --> 08:24.180
I won't forgive you, Okkotsu Yuuta!

08:24.180 --> 08:26.660
Not that I've ever even met you!

08:26.660 --> 08:28.030
That's misdirected anger.

08:28.030 --> 08:29.020
Salmon.

08:32.750 --> 08:33.520
Hey.

08:34.190 --> 08:35.480
They're here.

08:36.320 --> 08:40.470
Oh, look. It's everyone from Tokyo together.

08:42.350 --> 08:44.330
You went out of your way to greet us?

08:44.910 --> 08:46.330
Disgusting.

08:46.330 --> 08:48.340
Jujutsu Tech, Kyoto Second-Year
Zenin Mai

08:48.450 --> 08:50.840
Okkotsu's not here.

08:50.840 --> 08:52.840
Jujutsu Tech, Kyoto Third-Year
Toudou Aoi

08:52.990 --> 08:55.850
Shut up. Hurry up and hand over the cake box,

08:55.850 --> 08:58.140
and the yatsuhashi, kudzu noodles, 
and buckwheat cookies.

08:58.140 --> 08:59.240
Salmon.

08:59.240 --> 09:00.850
You guys hungry?

09:00.850 --> 09:03.040
Who is that first-year?

09:03.040 --> 09:03.850
She's scary.

09:03.850 --> 09:05.850
Jujutsu Tech, Kyoto Third-Year
Nishimiya Momo

09:05.950 --> 09:08.120
Never mind Okkotsu being absent.

09:08.120 --> 09:10.300
Isn't having two first-years a major handicap?

09:10.300 --> 09:11.360
A robot! It's a robot!

09:11.360 --> 09:13.360
Jujutsu Tech, Kyoto Second-Year
Ultimate Mechamaru

09:13.560 --> 09:16.360
Age is irrelevant to jujutsu sorcerers.

09:16.360 --> 09:18.370
Jujutsu Tech, Kyoto Third-Year
Kamo Noritoshi

09:18.490 --> 09:20.370
Especially with Fushiguro-kun.

09:20.760 --> 09:23.370
He's from the Zenin bloodline,

09:23.370 --> 09:25.880
but he's more talented 
than the head of the clan.

09:25.880 --> 09:26.500
Tsk.

09:26.820 --> 09:27.710
Something to say?

09:28.040 --> 09:29.080
Nope.

09:29.080 --> 09:30.300
Now, now...

09:30.300 --> 09:32.220
Please calm down, you two.

09:32.210 --> 09:34.210
Jujutsu Tech, Kyoto Second-Year
Miwa Kasumi

09:35.120 --> 09:36.180
Okay, now.

09:36.460 --> 09:38.140
Let's not fight amongst ourselves.

09:38.410 --> 09:40.600
My goodness, these children.

09:40.600 --> 09:42.600
Jujutsu Tech, Semi-First-Grade Sorcerer
Kyoto School Leader
Iori Utahime

09:42.720 --> 09:45.100
So, where's that idiot?

09:45.330 --> 09:46.770
Satoru's late.

09:46.770 --> 09:49.580
As if that idiot would ever show up on time.

09:49.580 --> 09:52.540
No one said "idiot" referred to Gojou-sensei.

09:56.490 --> 09:58.540
Sorry for the wait!

09:58.780 --> 10:01.040
Tsk. Gojou Satoru.

09:59.440 --> 10:01.040
Gojou Satoru!

10:02.000 --> 10:04.320
Hey, I see everyone's together.

10:04.320 --> 10:07.330
I was on a business trip overseas.

10:07.330 --> 10:09.970
So I will now hand out souvenirs!

10:09.970 --> 10:11.430
This is sudden.

10:11.430 --> 10:13.000
Sure it's not jet lag?

10:13.250 --> 10:16.880
Okay, everyone from Kyoto gets this 
protective charm from a particular tribe.

10:16.880 --> 10:18.130
None for you, Utahime.

10:18.130 --> 10:19.270
I don't need one!

10:19.510 --> 10:22.300
And for everyone from Tokyo, we have this!

10:24.400 --> 10:26.820
Overly excited adults are creepy.

10:30.390 --> 10:33.080
Hey! OPP!

10:33.080 --> 10:36.070
It's your departed friend, 
Itadori Yuuji-kun!

10:39.580 --> 10:41.080
Huh?!

10:41.080 --> 10:43.580
Huh? Huh?!

10:43.580 --> 10:46.540
They don't seem happy at all!

10:46.770 --> 10:48.480
N-No way.

10:48.480 --> 10:50.720
Okay, everyone from Kyoto!

10:50.720 --> 10:53.690
This is Sukuna's vessel, Itadori Yuuji-kun!

10:53.690 --> 10:55.550
Wh-What about the ones from Kyoto?

10:56.260 --> 10:58.550
They're too absorbed in their souvenirs!

11:00.860 --> 11:02.560
Sukuna's vessel?!

11:03.160 --> 11:05.560
What's the meaning of this?

11:05.560 --> 11:07.560
Jujutsu Tech, Kyoto School Principal
Gakuganji Yoshinobu

11:08.520 --> 11:10.560
Principal Gakuganji!

11:10.770 --> 11:13.560
Oh, thank goodness.

11:13.860 --> 11:18.870
I was worried you might 
just die from the shock.

11:20.020 --> 11:22.080
You damn brat!

11:27.540 --> 11:28.480
Hey.

11:28.480 --> 11:30.120
Uh, yes?

11:30.120 --> 11:32.160
You got something to say?

11:32.160 --> 11:32.960
Huh?

11:37.260 --> 11:41.950
I'm sorry for keeping quiet 
about being alive.

11:42.220 --> 11:45.010
Itadori Rejoins

11:47.220 --> 11:50.010
JUJUTSU KAISEN

11:52.680 --> 11:55.020
JUJUTSU KAISEN

11:55.270 --> 12:14.040
Jujutsu Technical High School
Tokyo-Kyoto Sister School Exchange Event

11:55.270 --> 12:14.040
Jujutsu Technical High School
Tokyo-Kyoto Sister School Exchange Event

11:58.850 --> 12:04.480
The Tokyo-Kyoto Sister School 
Exchange Event will be held over two days.

12:04.480 --> 12:07.300
The first day is a group battle...

12:07.700 --> 12:14.040
Wacky
Cursed Spirit Exorcism Race

12:09.880 --> 12:13.650
The Wacky Cursed Spirit Exorcism Race!

12:15.630 --> 12:17.330
The rules are simple.

12:16.920 --> 12:21.550
Second-Grade

12:17.610 --> 12:21.170
The first team to exorcise 
the second-grade cursed spirit

12:21.170 --> 12:24.050
released in the designated area wins.

12:24.440 --> 12:28.320
Several third-grade and lower cursed spirits 
will be released into the designated area, as well.

12:28.320 --> 12:31.120
If a winner is not decided by sundown,

12:31.120 --> 12:34.060
the team that exorcises the most wins.

12:34.320 --> 12:37.020
There are absolutely no other rules.

12:37.270 --> 12:40.480
Of course, you're welcome 
to sabotage the others,

12:40.480 --> 12:44.330
but remember, you're all on the same 
side in the fight against the curses.

12:44.650 --> 12:47.800
This exchange event will allow 
you to learn about yourselves

12:47.800 --> 12:50.030
and your comrades through competition.

12:50.960 --> 12:56.630
Be certain not to kill other competitors 
or injure them beyond recovery.

12:58.480 --> 12:59.420
That's it.

12:59.420 --> 13:02.910
You're all dismissed until the 
event commences at noon!

13:05.930 --> 13:09.140
\hTokyo Side Meeting\h

13:05.930 --> 13:09.140
\hTokyo Side Meeting\h

13:07.340 --> 13:09.130
Excuse me...

13:09.360 --> 13:12.060
Depending on how you look at it,

13:12.360 --> 13:14.990
this could be considered 
very extreme bullying.

13:14.990 --> 13:17.380
Shut up and stay that way for a while.

13:17.380 --> 13:18.440
Now, now...

13:18.660 --> 13:20.620
You heard his explanation.

13:20.620 --> 13:22.170
Cut him some slack.

13:22.430 --> 13:23.900
The panda talked!

13:24.120 --> 13:25.280
Salmon, salmon.

13:25.790 --> 13:26.860
What?

13:27.150 --> 13:29.640
Inumaki-senpai is a cursed speech user.

13:29.640 --> 13:33.330
Cursed speech is a technique that amplifies 
the power and compulsion of words.

13:33.560 --> 13:36.290
He limits his vocabulary to keep others safe.

13:36.580 --> 13:39.220
So if he told someone to 
go die, they'd actually die?

13:39.220 --> 13:40.580
That's really powerful.

13:40.580 --> 13:42.720
It's nothing that convenient.

13:43.010 --> 13:46.120
It's all case by case, depending 
on their difference in strength.

13:46.120 --> 13:49.530
If he uses powerful words, 
he's hit with massive feedback.

13:49.530 --> 13:51.840
Worst case, it could affect him.

13:52.250 --> 13:56.280
Limiting his vocabulary is a way 
for Toge to protect himself, as well.

13:57.660 --> 14:00.230
So how are you able to speak, Senpai?

14:00.230 --> 14:01.700
Are you some new breed of panda?

14:01.700 --> 14:04.240
Blabbing on about people's techniques...

14:04.240 --> 14:05.270
It's fine.

14:05.270 --> 14:07.510
Toge's isn't that kind of technique, anyway.

14:07.840 --> 14:09.830
More importantly, Yuuji...

14:10.740 --> 14:12.660
Give me back Slaughter Demon.

14:13.230 --> 14:15.020
You borrowed it from Satoru, right?

14:20.910 --> 14:22.380
Gimme!

14:22.700 --> 14:24.150
Here you go!

14:25.420 --> 14:27.590
I broke it.

14:27.590 --> 14:29.060
It's not coming back!

14:31.260 --> 14:34.880
Gojou-sensei... has it...

14:34.880 --> 14:37.330
Tsk, that blindfolded dumbass!

14:41.930 --> 14:43.320
Gross.

14:43.430 --> 14:45.620
So, what's the plan?

14:45.830 --> 14:48.810
The group battle format 
is what we expected,

14:48.810 --> 14:50.690
but we have another member now.

14:50.690 --> 14:53.090
Do we change strategies? 
There's not much time.

14:53.090 --> 14:54.110
Bonito flakes.

14:54.110 --> 14:55.620
Well, that depends on Yuuji.

14:55.800 --> 14:57.230
What can you do?

14:57.710 --> 14:59.100
Punch, kick...

14:59.100 --> 15:01.980
We have enough of that.

15:01.980 --> 15:03.070
Huh?

15:03.790 --> 15:07.590
I don't know what he's been 
doing since he's been dead,

15:07.990 --> 15:12.360
but if everyone from Tokyo and Kyoto 
fought him at once without cursed energy,

15:13.140 --> 15:14.890
Itadori would win.

15:15.420 --> 15:16.920
Oh?

15:17.610 --> 15:20.630
Megumi's saying that after fighting Toudou?

15:21.400 --> 15:23.230
That makes it convincing.

15:23.680 --> 15:25.280
Interesting.

15:29.400 --> 15:32.910
\hKyoto Side Meeting\h

15:29.400 --> 15:32.910
\hKyoto Side Meeting\h

15:29.900 --> 15:35.920
Kill Sukuna's vessel, Itadori Yuuji.

15:35.920 --> 15:37.920
He is not a person.

15:38.090 --> 15:40.230
So it will go unquestioned.

15:40.230 --> 15:42.250
It'll be treated as an accident.

15:42.250 --> 15:44.920
There's no need to hold back or hesitate.

15:45.120 --> 15:47.130
I don't want to...

15:47.130 --> 15:48.960
You say to kill him,

15:48.960 --> 15:51.920
but he's here because he didn't die, right?

15:52.140 --> 15:55.930
I've heard that Itadori's 
previous death was suicide.

15:56.130 --> 16:00.840
What is the one thing you must be cautious 
about when ending a hostile sorcerer?

16:00.840 --> 16:01.840
Kamo.

16:02.130 --> 16:02.940
Yes.

16:03.310 --> 16:06.240
You must kill them with cursed 
energy to prevent them from

16:06.240 --> 16:07.950
coming back as a curse after death.

16:08.230 --> 16:09.450
Exactly.

16:09.450 --> 16:14.020
If another delivers the finishing blow 
with cursed energy, then all is well.

16:14.020 --> 16:17.950
At present, Itadori Yuuji 
has control of the body.

16:17.950 --> 16:21.420
Unless Sukuna comes out, 
he's just a first-year.

16:21.420 --> 16:22.750
Killing him will be—

16:24.390 --> 16:26.620
This is stupid. Do what you want.

16:26.620 --> 16:28.090
Come back, Toudou.

16:28.740 --> 16:31.090
The principal isn't finished yet.

16:31.360 --> 16:36.010
Takada-chan's making a guest 
appearance on a walking show at 11.

16:36.010 --> 16:38.100
Do I need to explain any more?

16:38.330 --> 16:40.600
You can record it. Come back here.

16:40.850 --> 16:44.200
I'm going to watch the recording 
and watch it in real time!

16:44.670 --> 16:46.360
Who do you take me for?

16:48.780 --> 16:49.980
That's your problem here?!

16:49.980 --> 16:51.600
Listen, all of you.

16:51.600 --> 16:53.650
You listen, too, old man.

16:53.880 --> 16:58.660
I've long been disappointed in you all 
and your bad taste in women.

16:58.660 --> 17:01.340
Plot and scheme all you want on your own.

17:01.660 --> 17:04.660
But if you try to order me around again,

17:05.030 --> 17:06.680
I'll kill you.

17:10.830 --> 17:12.380
What do we do now?

17:12.670 --> 17:16.380
I don't think we'll be able to carry 
out the plan with him like that.

17:16.650 --> 17:18.810
The principal's gone off somewhere, too.

17:18.810 --> 17:21.860
I don't want to be killed by that guy.

17:21.860 --> 17:23.890
Does it even matter?

17:24.090 --> 17:27.790
He's going to go straight 
for the Tokyo team, anyway.

17:27.790 --> 17:29.920
If he's just going to go berserk,

17:29.920 --> 17:32.810
we can focus on the game.

17:33.130 --> 17:36.790
But we have to kill Itadori Yuuji, right?

17:37.100 --> 17:38.480
We're seriously doing this?

17:38.920 --> 17:42.460
I don't think he'll go as far as killing him.

17:42.460 --> 17:44.250
Though he probably could.

17:44.520 --> 17:47.050
Then we'll need someone to 
keep an eye on Toudou

17:47.050 --> 17:50.480
and deliver the final blow to Itadori Yuuji.

17:51.060 --> 17:52.410
I don't like this.

17:53.130 --> 17:56.380
We'll have cursed spirits to deal with, too, 
so we'll be in two-man cells anyway.

17:56.380 --> 17:58.000
That works out for us.

17:58.450 --> 17:59.230
No.

18:00.160 --> 18:02.740
Allowing a half-wit like Itadori Yuuji

18:02.740 --> 18:06.370
to be a sorcerer at Jujutsu Tech 
is a serious problem.

18:06.740 --> 18:08.770
One that goes beyond this exchange event.

18:09.230 --> 18:11.820
I cannot overlook this as the 
eldest son of the Kamo clan.

18:13.050 --> 18:16.820
We're all attacking Itadori Yuuji together.

18:17.690 --> 18:18.660
Hold on.

18:18.910 --> 18:22.620
What happens if Inumaki-kun 
is with Itadori-kun?

18:23.080 --> 18:27.510
Having all of us in one place is a risky 
move with that cursed speech user.

18:27.510 --> 18:30.600
Worst case, he could 
wipe us all out at once.

18:31.450 --> 18:33.100
That's true.

18:33.500 --> 18:38.140
No, if you know he's coming, 
he's not that scary to face.

18:38.430 --> 18:40.560
Let me have Maki.

18:40.560 --> 18:42.640
That brown-haired first-year, too, if possible.

18:42.850 --> 18:46.080
You're sounding just like Toudou.

18:48.880 --> 18:51.520
So what did you want?

18:51.880 --> 18:53.950
Huh? Why are you mad?

18:54.320 --> 18:56.440
I'm not mad, actually.

18:56.620 --> 18:59.630
Right? I haven't done anything, after all.

19:01.150 --> 19:06.320
There's someone working with either 
a curse user or curses at Jujutsu Tech.

19:07.600 --> 19:08.910
Impossible!

19:08.910 --> 19:11.310
A curse user might be one thing, 
but working with curses?

19:11.310 --> 19:14.880
A lot of them on that level 
have been popping up lately.

19:15.390 --> 19:19.380
They understand human speech, and they've 
formed a faction that's operating with purpose.

19:19.380 --> 19:22.890
They might think they're just 
working with a curse user, but...

19:23.930 --> 19:27.340
I'd like to ask you to handle 
investigating those at Kyoto, Utahime.

19:28.400 --> 19:31.360
What would you do if I was the traitor?

19:31.610 --> 19:32.920
No way.

19:32.920 --> 19:35.480
You're weak, and you don't have the guts—

19:38.160 --> 19:40.630
Scary! Hysterics won't win men, you know.

19:40.630 --> 19:43.450
I! Am! The senior here!

19:48.030 --> 19:49.020
Itadori.

19:50.340 --> 19:51.480
You okay?

19:51.740 --> 19:55.260
Yeah, sounds like I've got 
a big role, but I'll manage.

19:55.260 --> 19:56.380
I'm not talking about that.

19:56.860 --> 19:58.300
Something happened, right?

19:58.530 --> 20:00.300
Huh? Nothing happened.

20:03.520 --> 20:04.800
Okay, it did.

20:06.260 --> 20:09.320
But it's true that I'm fine.

20:10.590 --> 20:14.350
In fact, because of what happened, 
I don't want to lose to anyone.

20:15.280 --> 20:16.780
Okay, then.

20:17.160 --> 20:20.200
I don't really want to lose, either.

20:20.470 --> 20:21.980
What do you mean, "really"?

20:21.980 --> 20:24.190
You already got sent rolling around once!

20:24.190 --> 20:26.870
Overwhelm them! 
Let's thoroughly trounce them!

20:26.870 --> 20:28.170
For Maki-san's sake, too!

20:28.170 --> 20:29.860
Don't say stuff like that.

20:29.860 --> 20:30.980
Pollack roe.

20:30.980 --> 20:33.130
Yeah! For Maki-san's sake, too!

20:33.130 --> 20:35.130
Don't say stuff like that.

20:37.280 --> 20:38.790
Well, in that case,

20:39.490 --> 20:40.690
let's win!

20:42.230 --> 20:43.990
What are you doing taking the lead?

20:43.990 --> 20:45.010
Ow!

22:15.060 --> 22:17.560
Juju Stroll

22:17.560 --> 22:21.060
Sushi Eishuu

22:21.070 --> 22:26.510
Hello! Today we're here at the 
long-standing sushi shop, Eishuu!

22:26.930 --> 22:29.330
You should do that kind of thing, too.

22:29.330 --> 22:32.080
You'd be mad at me if I did.

22:33.630 --> 22:35.080
Welcome.

22:47.600 --> 22:50.380
What do you like, Takada-chan?

22:50.380 --> 22:53.640
Goatfish! And room temperature sake!

22:53.640 --> 22:55.310
They're great together!

22:55.310 --> 22:56.750
How old are you again?

22:56.750 --> 22:57.600
Huh?

23:01.860 --> 23:04.480
How long have you been making sushi, boss?

23:04.830 --> 23:06.780
I've been doing it since I was 20.

23:06.780 --> 23:11.260
Which means... about 300 years?

23:11.550 --> 23:12.870
Are you drunk?

23:13.200 --> 23:15.870
Here's the goatfish you ordered.

23:19.610 --> 23:21.900
Mm, it's so good!

23:21.900 --> 23:23.970
Can I have yours, too?

23:23.970 --> 23:25.380
Of course not.

23:27.480 --> 23:28.920
Sorry!

23:28.920 --> 23:30.570
Honestly, what are you thinking?

23:30.570 --> 23:32.770
Well, it just looked so delicious!

23:31.480 --> 23:33.270
She's drunk.

23:33.270 --> 23:35.390
Tan, Taka-tan!

23:33.270 --> 23:35.390
That's my Takada-chan.

23:35.730 --> 23:38.640
Sensei, did you know "OPP" 
actually stands for something?

23:38.640 --> 23:40.540
Huh? It does?

23:40.540 --> 23:43.240
Ocean Pacific Peace.

23:43.240 --> 23:44.350
Seriously?

23:51.570 --> 23:55.030
Episode 15:
Kyoto Sister School Exchange Event - Group Battle 1 -
